    <h1>Loyalty and Strategy</h1>

    <div class="project-meta-list">
      <p><span class="meta-label">Role:</span> Lead Product Designer &amp; Growth Strategist</p>
      <p><span class="meta-label">Focus Ecosystem:</span> CVS ExtraCare &amp; ExtraCare Plus (80M+ Active Members)</p>
      <p><span class="meta-label">Core Impact:</span> Engineered high-conversion user experiences that unlocked millions in incremental margin, eliminated multi-platform friction, and drove daily active engagement through gamification.</p>
    </div>

    <p class="project-intro">As the design lead for the Loyalty and Consumer Growth workstream, my mission was to transform transactional touch-points into relational experiences. By identifying friction points in user journeys and introducing data-driven UX patterns, my team successfully optimized acquisition, retention, and lifetime value across physical and digital storefronts.</p>

    <!-- Hero Banner -->
    <img src="/images/lnp/live_01.jpg" alt="Loyalty and Strategy Overview" class="project-image" />

      <h2>Case Study: Single-Data Point ExtraCare Enrollment</h2>

      <h3>The Challenge</h3>
      <p>Around 54% of in-store transactions at CVS happen at Self-Checkout. Of these transactions, roughly 60% are not ExtraCare linked. The value of an ExtraCare membership is not highlighted at self checkout, nor is there currently a way to easily unlock these savings. Customers needed to abandon their transaction, approach a colleague and enroll with them, or lose out on savings. This massive friction caused staggering drop-off rates.</p>

      <h3>The UX Intervention</h3>
      <p>I led the design of a brand new SCO enrollment flow, making the entire process a single, high-intent data point (just the phone number). By leveraging a seamless .com flow, OTP validation and an SMS strategy, we deferred the rest of the profile setup to a later digital touchpoint.</p>

